          "title": "The Future of Routing w/ Tanner Linsley",
          "duration": "4:34:24",
          "channel": "Ryan Carniato",
          "description": "Tanner is back to talk all things routing. We will catch up on his progress on Tanstack Router, talk about TypeScript, look at how data fetching and server rendering play a part and talk about where things are heading.\n\n[0:00] Preamble\n[5:30] Welcome Tanner Linsley\n[12:15] Routing & TypeScript - Why TanStack Router?\n[17:15] getParentRoute & Advanced TypeScript Inference\n[22:30] Relative Routing & Link\n[27:30] Declaration Merging - Extending the Register Interface\n[33:00] TanStack: A Framework for Client-Focused React Apps\n[42:00] File System Routing & Code Generation\n[59:00] Server-Side Rendering & the Stream Transform\n[1:06:00] Routing in React vs. Reactive Routing\n[1:11:00] Data-Fetching in Tanstack Router\n[1:20:00] Q&A: Browser APIs? Timeline? SearchParam Routing? \n[1:25:00] Farewell Tanner Linsley & More SearchParam Routing\n[1:34:00] Cache/Preload Architecture: RFC & Demo\n[1:50:00] Cache/Preload: Simple Examples\n[2:00:00] Cache/Preload: Hackernews\n[2:09:15] Cache/Preload: createAsync & Composing Primitives\n[2:19:30] Revisiting Partials\n[2:32:30] This Week in JavaScript: Data Fetching Debate\n[2:45:00] TWiJ: TanStack News & Browser Standards Discussion\n[2:51:30] TWiJ: Ryan Florence on Focus Events & flushSync()\n[2:58:00] TWiJ: Rick Hanlon on React Documentation Philosophy\n[3:05:30] TWiJ: Tauri, Brendan_CSEL's Migrations, & Alpine.js\n[3:14:00] TWiJ: Qwik's New Astro Integration & astro-remix\n[3:20:30] TWiJ: Next 14 & Partial Pre-Rendering\n[3:25:45] TWiJ: Netlify's New Features\n[3:32:30] TWiJ: MobX's Decorators & Qwik's Serialization\n[3:39:00] TWiJ: Closure Extraction in Server Actions\n[3:46:45] TWiJ: Using .bind() as an Alternative\n[4:02:00] TWiJ: Jason Lengstorf's Recent Content & MobX Again\n[4:06:00] Q&A: SolidStart, Nitro & Bundle Size\n[4:15:00] Q&A: React, State Management & MVC\n[4:21:00] Q&A: DHH & No-Build\n[4:29:00] Conclusion\n\nThanks to @zombiefacesupreme for the timestamps.",
